\fBripwire-rs\fR is a high-throughput context router and deterministic static analysis engine designed for AI coding agents, developer CLI workflows, and automated CI/CD safety gates. It is a Rust port and rewrite of \fBredhat-et/ripwire\fR, originally authored by David Brewster.
.PP
It indexes codebases across 36 programming languages using multi-threaded parallel Tree-Sitter grammar queries, extracts language-agnostic embedded SQL table lineage from application string literals without extra flags, builds a resolved workspace call graph with multi-tier scoping precedence, executes Personalized PageRank over compressed sparse row (CSR) transpose matrices with dangling node mass redistribution, and streams dense, token-budgeted XML representations to stdout.
Output formats are minified, self-documenting XML designed to maximize LLM in-context reasoning efficiency while eliminating hallucinated code dependencies and false-negative omissions.

Budget flags are shaping ceilings, not hard gates: output is shaped to fit. \fB\-\-pack\-task\fR reports \fBover_budget=1\fR and \fB\-\-recall\fR reports \fBover_ceiling=1\fR only when the minimal unit alone cannot fit. \fB\-\-recall\fR admits \fI5*N/2\fR bytes for \fB\-\-max\-tokens=N\fR; \fB\-\-for\fR windows its ranked symbols by the token budget (default 4000 tokens), with \fB\-\-limit\fR / \fB\-\-offset\fR overriding the window.
.SH ORIENTATION & BUDGET OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-top\-k= N
Retain only the \fIN\fR highest-ranked symbols in the emitted symbol map (e.g. \fB\-\-top\-k=200\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-tokens= N
Budget the output to approximately \fIN\fR LLM prompt tokens (~4 bytes per token).
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-budget= N
Alias for \fB\-\-max\-tokens\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-pack\-budget= BYTES
Streaming budget cap in raw bytes (default: 65536 = 64 KB).
.TP
.BI \-\-rank\-by= MODE
Ranking signal algorithm: \fBpagerank\fR (default), \fBauthority\fR, \fBhub\fR, \fBdegree\fR, \fBccx\fR, or \fBstable\fR. Unknown signals are errors.
.TP
.BI \-\-legend= MODE
Schema documentation comment posture: \fBcompact\fR (default, includes in-context AST schema header comment) or \fBnone\fR (suppresses leading XML comments).
.TP
.B \-\-legend\-dict
Emit full schema legend dictionary explaining all XML and JSON tags and attribute abbreviations.
.TP
.B \-\-stable
Emit deterministic path-ordered symbol map omitting volatile rank attributes.

.SH DETAIL LADDER & BODY OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-expand= SYMS
Expand full source body of comma-separated symbols \fISYMS\fR and list callee signatures.
.TP
.BI \-\-outline= SYMS
Outline control-flow skeletons of symbols (declarations, loops, branches with body statements collapsed).
.TP
.BI \-\-pack\-top\-n= N
Pack source bodies of the top \fIN\fR highest PageRank symbols.
.TP
.B \-\-tree
Orient file by file, showing each file's top 3 symbols by rank.
.TP
.B \-\-report
Generate executive Markdown architecture report summarizing symbols, connectivity, and quality health. The default is bounded to 16 KiB, shared equally by five lists (modules, bridges, god files, dependency cycles, top symbols); each list states \fI(showing S of T)\fR. Page with \fB\-\-limit\fR and \fB\-\-offset\fR; a capped list prints a \fBnext\fR route.

.SH NAVIGATION & GRAPH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-callers= SYM
Query direct 1-hop incoming callers of symbol \fISYM\fR. For database tables, lists all functions and methods querying or mutating the table across all host languages.
.TP
.BI \-\-callees= SYM
Query direct 1-hop outgoing callees called by symbol \fISYM\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-impact= SYM
Compute transitive blast radius (reachability graph) reaching symbol \fISYM\fR across code and database schema migrations.
Unbound candidate call sites appear separately as \fB<dc>\fR rows and are not graph edges. A capped candidate list reports \fBdc_shown\fR of \fBdeclined_calls\fR; raise \fB\-\-token-budget\fR to show more.
.TP
.BI \-\-impact\-depth= N
Optional impact traversal depth limit, matching MCP \fBmax_depth\fR. Global; also works with \fBnavigate --impact\fR. The default traversal is unchanged.
.TP
.BI \-\-uses= SYM
Query all static use-sites (calls, definitions, reads, writes, imports, extends) of symbol \fISYM\fR, including cross-language embedded SQL table lineage from application string literals.
All indexed sites are shown by default. Use \fB\-\-limit=N \-\-offset=M\fR for a path-and-line ordered window; \fBnext_offset\fR advances the window.
Bare non-local variable reads are indexed for Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, and Rust; declarations, assignment targets, labels, and lexical shadows are excluded. Unsupported binding forms remain evidence floors.
.TP
.BI \-\-find\-symbol= SYM
Query both incoming callers and outgoing callees of symbol \fISYM\fR in one view.
.TP
.BI \-\-connect= A,B,...
Compute the minimal connecting subgraph relating 2 to 16 named symbols.
.TP
.BI \-\-path= A:B ", " \-\-path\-between= A:B
Find the shortest directed call path from source symbol \fIA\fR to destination \fIB\fR (\fIA:B\fR or \fIA,B\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-with\-graph
Include resolved call-graph edges in task and retrieval output.

.SH SEARCH & RETRIEVAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-for= TASK
Task-lens relevance ranking: retrieves ranked declarations, signatures, and context relevant to natural-language task description \fITASK\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-grep= PAT
Search for literal trigram text pattern \fIPAT\fR; every match is annotated with its enclosing AST symbol.
Span tiers distinguish code, comments, and strings. \fB\-\-grep\-in=any\fR includes all tiers; \fB\-\-in=PATH\fR restricts paths. Repeat \fB\-\-and=PAT\fR and \fB\-\-not=PAT\fR to combine literal terms; \fB\-\-grep\-scope=file\fR applies them across the entire file instead of the matched line. Off-index text hits are reported separately.
.TP
.BI \-\-whereis= SYM
Locate which branches, revisions, or tree locations define symbol \fISYM\fR.
Scans HEAD and local branch trees, reading each distinct blob up to 2 MiB once. Changed and untracked worktree paths replace the corresponding HEAD rows; a subdirectory root scopes every tree scan.
.TP
.BI \-\-mentions= SYM
Locate Markdown documentation and specification files that reference symbol \fISYM\fR in backticks.
.TP
.BI \-\-exemplar= TASK|KIND
Retrieve best-in-class existing implementation of kind or role to imitate.
.TP
.BI \-\-lego= TYPE
Show one interface or trait contract and all implementing types in the codebase.
.TP
.BI \-\-recall= TASK
Search repository documentation, design plans, and notes for relevant concepts.
.TP
.BI \-\-from\-trace= FILE
Map stack trace lines, compiler error messages, or sanitizer frames onto indexed symbols.
.TP
.B \-\-owners
Analyze recency-weighted Git commit authorship and calculate per-file bus-factor metrics.
.TP
.BI \-\-grep\-in= DIR
Restrict trigram text search to files whose path matches substring \fIDIR\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-grep\-scope= SCOPE
Restrict trigram text search to hits enclosed inside symbol or namespace \fISCOPE\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-and= PAT
Conjunction filter for search: require matches to also contain pattern \fIPAT\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-not= PAT
Negation filter for search: exclude matches containing pattern \fIPAT\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-in= SCOPE
Scope filter: require matches to be located inside enclosing symbol, class, or directory \fISCOPE\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-handles
Emit compact opaque refetch handles on retrieval rows for low-token follow-ups.
.TP
.BI \-\-refetch [= HANDLE ]
With \fIHANDLE\fR, expand a compact refetch handle previously emitted by \fB\-\-handles\fR. Bare, when the root is a remote git URL, clone it fresh instead of reusing the cached clone.
.TP
.BI \-\-sections= LIST
With \fB\-\-for\fR, restore the \fB<lego>\fR section (interfaces declared in the ranked files, with their implementors) that the bundle collapses to a counted stub \fB<lego total= shown="0" capped="1" next=>\fR by default. \fILIST\fR is a closed, comma-separated set of \fBlego\fR and \fBcompose\fR, each at most once; \fBcompose\fR (HAS-A member-field rows) is accepted but never produced because this build does not index member fields. Refused without \fB\-\-for\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-help\-task= TASK
Recommend the single best ripwire-rs command for natural-language task \fITASK\fR with repository-fact evidence (\fBgit\fR, \fBdirty\fR, \fBtrace\fR, \fBresolved_symbols\fR), integer score/margin, and honest abstention.

.SH VERIFICATION & SAFETY GATES
.TP
.BI \-\-edit\-check= SYM
Verify caller compatibility after modifying symbol \fISYM\fR's signature. Verifies parameter count and visibility changes against git \fBHEAD\fR across all 1-hop callers. \fB\-\-limit\fR/\fB\-\-offset\fR page the compatible caller rows; incompatible callers always print.
.TP
.BI \-\-affected= PATH
Transitive reachability mapping from changed file or symbol \fIPATH\fR to affected test suites, ranked by evidence distance. Tests named after a changed file (\fBtest_X\fR, \fBX_test\fR, \fBX_spec\fR, \fBX.test\fR, \fBX.spec\fR; \fBXTest\fR in a test dir for Java, Kotlin, C#, PHP) are listed with \fBpartner="1"\fR; a file with several candidates gets none.
.TP
.BI \-\-test\-gate [=FILES]
Pre-PR verification gate: names tests to run and untested blast radius. Exits with code \fB4\fR if non-empty obligations exist. Defaults to git diff.
.TP
.BI \-\-situ [=FILES]
Canonical \fBripwire-rs.situ/v1\fR XML report for a change: blast radius, tests to run, and Fowler's Shotgun Surgery co-change coupling. Defaults to git diff.
.TP
.BI \-\-safe\-delete= SYM
Safe deletion assessment: joins 1-hop callers, impact blast radius, test coverage, and dead code candidate status for symbol \fISYM\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-exercises= TESTFILE
Show which non-test domain symbols a specific test harness file reaches.
.TP
.B \-\-quality\-baseline
Pin a code quality baseline stamped with git \fBHEAD\fR to \fB.ripwire-rs_quality_baseline\fR. On a dirty tree that already holds gating findings against \fBHEAD\fR, refuses (exit \fB1\fR) and names the first finding.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-dirty
With \fB\-\-quality\-baseline\fR, pin anyway; the sidecar records \fBdirty 1\fR and \fBabsorbed N\fR, and every later \fB\-\-quality\-delta\fR against it carries \fBbaseline_absorbed="N"\fR. Refused alone.
.TP
.BI \-\-quality\-delta [=REV]
Measure code quality regressions against git \fBHEAD\fR (or pinned baseline) across 10 facets (cognitive complexity, cyclomatic complexity, dead code, duplicates, nesting, params, churn, and arity breaks). Exits non-zero (\fB2\fR) if gating regressions are detected. With \fB=\fR\fIREV\fR (or \fIREV\fR\fB..HEAD\fR) the baseline is rebuilt from the merge base of \fIREV\fR and \fBHEAD\fR instead, with no sidecar: the report carries \fBbaseline="git-ref"\fR and \fBbase_ref=\fR. The value needs \fB=\fR, so \fB\-\-quality\-delta .\fR still names the path.
.TP
.B \-\-map\-diff
Re-rank the architecture map toward git-changed files so recent work automatically floats to the top of the context window.
.TP
.B \-\-seams
Discover untested cross-module call boundaries (integration seams) across directory and subsystem boundaries.
.TP
.BI \-\-pr\-context [=BASE]
Generate a composite pull request review context bundle against base reference \fIBASE\fR (default: \fBmain\fR or \fBmaster\fR), including changed symbols, impact, tests, co-change, and authors.
.TP
.BI \-\-merge\-scout= REFS
Symbol-level overlap of each ref in \fIREFS\fR against HEAD: the functions, methods and types each ref changed since its merge base with HEAD, the symbols two refs both changed (conflicts), files both changed without a shared symbol (risks), each arm's overlap with HEAD, and a landing order (fewest conflicts first). Read-only; an unknown ref exits with code \fB1\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-arch= FILE
Enforce architectural layering rules from file \fIFILE\fR. Exits with code \fB2\fR if any forbidden cross-layer call dependency is introduced.
.TP
.B \-\-mermaid
Export a Mermaid flowchart diagram of module call dependency topology to stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-zoom [=\fIDEPTH\fR]
Multi-level Louvain module hierarchy over the call graph. \fBlevels=\fR is the computed depth (level 0 is the finest partition); the top \fB2\fR levels print by default, and modules at the cut carry \fBchildren=\fIK\fR. \fIDEPTH\fR keeps only the finest \fIDEPTH\fR levels. Top modules are windowed at 40 (\fB\-\-limit\fR/\fB\-\-offset\fR page them).
.TP
.BI \-\-zoom\-levels= N
With \fB\-\-zoom\fR, print \fIN\fR levels from the top (\fB0\fR = every level). Refused alone.
.TP
.B \-\-biggest\-first
Rank functions by readability volume and physical size, largest first.
.TP
.B \-\-nonlocal\-state
Detect functions reading or mutating reachable global or file-static state. Immutable scalar constants are not state; a constant object or array is state only when the indexed files mutate it (property write, delete, or an in-place method such as push).
.TP
.B \-\-lint
Scan codebase for AST code smells (complexity spikes, deep nesting, dead functions).
.TP
.B \-\-lint\-catalog
Print built-in AST code smell catalog with severity rankings.
.TP
.BI \-\-lint\-select= RULES
Select comma-separated AST lint rule prefixes to run (e.g. \fBlarge-function,deep-nesting\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-lint\-ignore= RULES
Ignore specific comma-separated AST lint rules during lint scan.
.TP
.B \-\-naming\-calibration
Calibrate naming consistency lens rules against git rename history.
.BI \-\-at= FILE:LINE
Resolve innermost symbol definition enclosing \fIFILE:LINE\fR. Exits 1 if no symbol spans line.
.TP
.BI \-\-verify= CLAIM
Formally verify a closed-world code claim across 6 shapes (\fBcalls(A,B)\fR, \fBuses(SYM)\fR, \fBunused(SYM)\fR, \fBcontains(FILE,"LIT")\fR, \fBdefines(FILE,SYM)\fR, \fBreaches(SYM,"FILE"|LAYER)\fR), emitting inline witness rows and a 3-valued verdict (\fBconfirmed\fR, \fBrefuted\fR, \fBnot-established\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-pack\-task= TASK
Assemble single-call orientation task bundle under budget tailored to task description. Compose with \fB\-\-partition=N\fR (\fIN\fR=2..16) to carve 1 shared core plus \fIN\fR Louvain-community subagent slices.
.TP
.BI \-\-graph\-query= QUERY
Evaluate functional graph query expression (e.g. \fBcallers(main)\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Run self-check diagnostics, verifying grammar integrity, git health, and baseline presence.
.TP
.B \-\-notes
Display pinned session gotchas and notes.
.TP
.BI \-\-note\-add= NOTE
Append a pinned session gotcha note.
.TP
.BI \-\-replace\-symbol\-body= BODY
Atomically replace an entire symbol definition with new source code body.
.TP
.BI \-\-insert\-before\-symbol= TEXT
Atomically insert source code immediately before a symbol definition.
.TP
.BI \-\-insert\-after\-symbol= TEXT
Atomically insert source code immediately after a symbol definition.
.TP
.BI \-\-edit\-target\-file= FILE
Specify target file to disambiguate symbol during atomic code replacement.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-post\-check
Skip post-edit contract, arity, and syntax verification.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-remote\-edits
Allow atomic symbol edits when connected over remote network transport.
.TP
.B \-\-baseline
Pin architectural baseline sidecar stamped with git \fBHEAD\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-baseline\-update
Update architectural baseline sidecar with newly introduced violations.
.TP
.B \-\-pin\-census
Pin quality census snapshot.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope= SCOPE
Partition \fB\-\-quality\-delta\fR analysis by author or team ownership scope \fISCOPE\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-cochange\-groups
Cluster co-changing files into multi-file change groups.
.TP
.BI \-\-cochange\-recur= K
Minimum sub-window recurrence count threshold for co-change pairs (default: 2).
.TP
.BI \-\-partition [=K]
Partition codebase into \fIK\fR cohesive module clusters, or compose with \fB\-\-pack\-task\fR to emit \fB<ctx\-partitions>\fR for \fIK\fR parallel subagents.
.TP
.BI \-\-plan\-lanes [=N]
Plan \fIN\fR parallel worktree lanes before writing code (with \fB\-\-task=GOAL\fR or \fB\-\-brief=FILE\fR), reporting per-lane symbol claims, pairwise conflicts, same-file risk, contract touches, and greedy fewest-conflicts-first landing order as 1-line JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-brief= FILE
Explicit per-lane brief file for \fB\-\-plan\-lanes\fR (one non-blank task line per lane).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-stable
Disable stable dependency violation warnings in \fB\-\-deps\fR output.
.SH ARCHITECTURE & CODE INTELLIGENCE
.TP
.B \-\-dead\-code
Detect internal functions with zero incoming callers across the repository.
.TP
.B \-\-communities
Partition call graph into cohesive modular clusters using Louvain community detection.
.TP
.BI \-\-community= ID
Inspect member symbols and bridges of a specific community cluster.
.TP
.BI \-\-around= SYM
Extract ego-graph around symbol \fISYM\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-around\-depth= N
Depth limit for \fB\-\-around\fR ego-graph (default: 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-around\-fanout= N
Maximum neighbors explored per hop for \fB\-\-around\fR (default: 32).
.TP
.B \-\-external\-surface
Discover symbols referenced in code that have no definition in the repository (standard library and external package surface).
.TP
.B \-\-deps
Generate file-to-file dependency graph with afferent and efferent inclusion counts.
.TP
.B \-\-clones
Detect AST code duplication and near-miss duplicate functions across Type-1 (exact), Type-2 (renamed identifiers), and Type-3 (gapped modifications) clone categories.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-tokens= N
Minimum token length threshold for clone candidate extraction (default: 40).
.TP
.B \-\-hotspots
Rank repository files by maintenance risk score, combining commit churn with Campbell cognitive complexity.
.TP
.B \-\-cochange
Mine historical Git co-change coupling to identify hidden file coupling (Fowler's Shotgun Surgery).
.TP
.BI \-\-since= DATE_OR_REV
Limit Git history traversal to commits after this date (YYYY-MM-DD) or revision.
.TP
.BI \-\-slice= SYM[:VAR]
Perform ARISE intra-procedural def-use variable dataflow slicing for variable \fIVAR\fR inside symbol \fISYM\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-slice\-flow= DIRECTION
Dataflow direction for \fB\-\-slice\fR: \fBfwd\fR (default, forward dependencies), \fBback\fR (backward origins), or \fBboth\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-slice\-depth= N
Maximum hop depth for ARISE intra-procedural def-use variable dataflow slice (default: 8).
.B \-\-flags
Scan codebase for dark feature gates, environment reads, and compile-time flags.
.TP
.B \-\-doc\-drift
Detect stale or broken symbol references within repository documentation.
.TP
.B \-\-stray\-content
Track authored content living on divergent branches that has not merged into \fBHEAD\fR.

.SH MODIFIERS & BATCHING
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON instead of XML for navigation and query commands, preserving hierarchy, root tag/attributes/items, and text/CDATA. Leaf text uses \fBtext\fR; mixed text is interleaved in \fBitems\fR. Reserved-name attributes use \fBattributes\fR; namespaced names use \fB{uri}local\fR. Malformed reports fail explicitly.
.TP
.BI \-\-batch= FILE
Execute at most 16 shared read sub-queries from \fIname:argument\fR or \fIname:{JSON arguments}\fR lines (\fI-\fR for stdin); ignore blank/comment lines. More than 16 is a whole-batch error. Individual failures emit \fB<error>\fR; recursive batches and writes (including quality baseline and quality-delta acknowledgment options) are rejected per item.
.TP
.BI \-\-add\-skills [=DIR]
Install 17 pre-packaged ripwire-rs agent skills and active manifest (\fB.ripwire\-rs\-manifest\-v1\fR) to \fI~/.agents/skills\fR (or custom \fIDIR\fR). Replaces stale or broken symlinks safely. Alias: \fB\-\-install\-skills\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude= GLOB
Exclude glob or directory pattern from crawling and indexing. Repeatable; each value may also be a comma-separated list.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ignore
Do not respect \fB.gitignore\fR rules during directory traversal.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-tests
Exclude test files and test directories from analysis.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-file\-size= BYTES
Maximum file size in bytes to index (default: 2 MB).
.TP
.BI \-\-scip= FILE
Overlay a compiler\-backed SCIP index: call sites it resolves bind exactly (\fBprov="scip"\fR, map header \fBprecise=K\fR), sites it resolves outside the index count as external, and every other site keeps name resolution. Bypasses the cache.
Also supported by \fBnavigate\fR, plain and task-ranked \fBorient\fR, and \fBmcp\fR (including \fB\-\-mcp\fR). MCP retains the indexed graph for the session. Unreadable or malformed indexes fail explicitly without a name-only fallback.
The option is global and may appear before or after a subcommand. Multiline calls match the callee identifier's index line; reported call-site lines preserve the call expression's start.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-redact
Disable secret redaction on emitted code snippets.
.TP
.B \-\-compress
Compress output using compact token dialect.
.TP
.BI \-\-index\-out= FILE
Cold-parse the tree, write the analysis cache to \fIFILE\fR and exit without a map; reload it with \fB\-\-cache=\fR\fIFILE\fR while HEAD, the working tree and the binary match. Refuses \fB\-\-exclude\fR, \fB\-\-no\-ignore\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\-tests\fR, \fB\-\-max\-file\-size\fR and \fB\-\-scip\fR, which bypass the cache.
.TP
.B \-\-lsp
Launch stdio JSON-RPC Language Server Protocol (LSP) server bridge supporting \fBinitialize\fR, \fBtextDocument/definition\fR, \fBtextDocument/references\fR, \fBtextDocument/documentSymbol\fR, and \fBtextDocument/hover\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-pretty
Pretty-print indented XML output (default is minified token-optimized single-line XML).
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp\-token= TOKEN
Require authentication token \fITOKEN\fR for MCP transport.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-inventory
Drop the unranked file inventory tier from ranked map and metrics output.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-memory= N [K|M|G]
Enforce an explicit RSS memory ceiling (or set via \fBRIPWIRE_MAX_MEMORY\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-lint\-max\-per\-rule= N
Cap the maximum findings emitted per AST lint rule.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-stale
With \fB\-\-quality\-delta\fR, print every stale \fB.ripwire-rs_quality_acks\fR row. Without it, a regression-free delta collapses those rows to \fBstale_by_kind=\fR and a \fBstale_next=\fR replay. Refused alone.
.TP
.B \-\-whereis\-full\-text
Emit verbatim matched lines in \fB\-\-whereis\fR without length truncation.
.TP
.BI \-\-whereis\-listing= MODE
Filter \fB\-\-whereis\fR results by \fBdefs\fR, \fBrefs\fR, or \fBall\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp\-tools= LIST
Restrict exposed MCP tools to a comma-separated list or profile (\fBcore\fR, \fBfull\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-agent= AGENT
Target agent profile for output token shaping and syntax formatting.
.TP
.BI \-\-with\-profile= FILE
Annotate code symbols with runtime performance profile weights from \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-run\-trace= CMD
Execute runtime trace command \fICMD\fR and map executed frames onto indexed symbols.
.TP
.BI \-\-run\-timeout= SEC
Timeout in seconds for \fB\-\-run\-trace\fR execution (default: 30).
.TP
.B \-\-eval\-mined
Run evaluation benchmark against mined git commits.
.TP
.B \-\-eval\-skills
Run agent skill effectiveness evaluation benchmark.
.TP
.B \-\-eval\-stray
Run cross-branch divergent stray content evaluation benchmark.
.TP
.BI \-\-eval\-scip= FILE
Score name-based call resolution against the compiler-backed SCIP index \fIFILE\fR: every call site the index pins is resolved again without SCIP and classified exact, split-hit, wrong, missed, external-agreed, false-edge or unindexed (an edge the index calls external into a file it holds no document for, such as \fB.js\fR beside a TypeScript-only index; left out of precision), with precision, recall, per-reason counts for each disagreeing class (the edge's provenance, or declined, unresolved, external, builtin, ignored) and sampled disagreements per class and reason. Refuses \fB\-\-scip\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-eval\-samples= N
Sampled disagreements per class and reason for \fB\-\-eval\-scip\fR (default 10).
.SH VISUALIZATION OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-html [=FILE]
Export interactive, self-contained SVG/HTML call graph visualization (writes to stdout or specified file).
.TP
.BI \-\-color\-by= MODE
Node coloring mode for HTML visualization: \fBlang\fR (default), \fBcommunity\fR, \fBcx\fR (complexity), \fBchurn\fR, or \fBtested\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-export= FILE
Write the resolved call graph to \fIFILE\fR: \fB.graphml\fR (Gephi, yEd, Neo4j APOC) or \fB.json\fR (node-link, NetworkX/D3). Nodes carry name, kind, file, line, lang and rank; edges carry \fBprov\fR (how the edge bound) and \fBtype_use\fR. Prints one \fB<export>\fR summary row.

.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B ripwire-rs orient \fR[\fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-for\fR \fITASK\fR] [\fB\-\-scip\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Exploration and task-based context orientation.
.TP
.B ripwire-rs navigate \fR[\fIPATH\fR] \fB\-\-symbol\fR \fISYM\fR [\fB\-\-callers\fR|\fB\-\-callees\fR|\fB\-\-impact\fR] [\fB\-\-scip\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Symbol neighborhood analysis and traversals.
.TP
.B ripwire-rs gate \fR[\fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-edit\-check\fR|\fB\-\-affected\fR|\fB\-\-quality\-delta\fR|\fB\-\-test\-gate\fR]
Pre-commit verification safety gates.
.TP
.B ripwire-rs metrics \fR[\fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-hotspots\fR|\fB\-\-clones\fR]
Code health and structural complexity metrics.
.TP
.B ripwire-rs slice \fR[\fIPATH\fR] \fB\-\-symbol\fR \fISYM\fR \fB\-\-var\fR \fIVAR\fR
Intra-procedural def-use slicing.
.TP
.B ripwire-rs mcp \fR[\fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-scip\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Launch native Model Context Protocol (MCP) JSON-RPC 2.0 server over standard input/output.
Overlapping tools return canonical CLI XML/text in \fBresult.content[0].text\fR, with identical facts, defaults, errors, and limits; no bespoke JSON summaries. Architecture maps default to 200 symbols and 65536 bytes. Connecting subgraphs default to radius 2. Slicing shares CLI workspace-root and flow/depth errors.
MCP batch success entries retain \fBtool/result/kind\fR (\fBxml|text|json\fR); malformed names fail per item. The CLI embeds XML and escapes text/JSON results. MCP \fBowners\fR accepts integer \fBdetail > 0\fR; \fBwhereis\fR accepts \fBlisting=defs|refs|all\fR and boolean \fBfull_text\fR, rejecting invalid listings. Detail 2 serves all requested bodies with accurate \fBshown/total\fR.
.TP
.B ripwire-rs skills \fR[\fIDIR\fR]
Install and manage 17 ripwire-rs agent skills into the cross-agent discovery directory (default: \fI~/.agents/skills\fR).
.SH SYMBOL SELECTOR SYNTAX
When querying symbols via \fB\-\-callers\fR, \fB\-\-callees\fR, \fB\-\-impact\fR, \fB\-\-uses\fR, \fB\-\-expand\fR, or \fB\-\-edit\-check\fR, \fBripwire-rs\fR accepts several selector formats:
.TP
.B bare_name
Matches any symbol with name \fIbare_name\fR (e.g. \fBlen\fR).
.TP
.B Scope::name
Disambiguates by enclosing type or namespace scope (e.g. \fBInterner::len\fR or \fBType.method\fR).
.TP
.B file_path:name
Disambiguates by file path prefix/suffix and symbol name (e.g. \fBsrc/domain.rs:len\fR).
.TP
.B file_path::Scope::name
Fully qualified canonical identifier (e.g. \fBsrc/domain.rs::Interner::len\fR).
.TP
.B file_path:LINE
Picks the definition starting nearest at or above \fILINE\fR in that file (e.g. \fBsrc/domain.rs:42\fR).

.SH EXAMPLES
Analyze a remote repository (\fIPATH\fR may be an \fBhttps://\fR, \fBssh://\fR, or \fBgit@\fR URL; it is shallow-cloned once into \fI$TMPDIR/ripwire-rs/\fR and reused until \fB\-\-refetch\fR):
.RS
.B ripwire-rs https://github.com/org/repo \-\-report
.RE
.PP
Expand full body of an interned method:
.RS
.B ripwire-rs . \-\-expand="Interner::len"
.RE
.PP
Query cross-language read and write lineage for an embedded SQL database table:
.RS
.B ripwire-rs . \-\-uses="user_accounts"
.RE
.PP
Run pre-PR test gate check (exits 4 on untested blast radius):
.RS
.B ripwire-rs . \-\-test\-gate
.RE
.PP
Inspect situational awareness diff analysis:
.RS
.B ripwire-rs . \-\-situ
.RE
.PP
Verify whether a symbol can be safely deleted:
.RS
.B ripwire-rs . \-\-safe\-delete="Interner::len"
.RE
.PP
Partition repository call graph into modules:
.RS
.B ripwire-rs . \-\-communities
.RE
.PP
Find dead internal functions:
.RS
.B ripwire-rs . \-\-dead\-code
.RE
.PP
Execute a batch of queries in a single turn:
.RS
.B ripwire-rs . \-\-batch=queries.txt
.RE

